      "content": "Those are getting closer, but they still feel a bit polite. If my student wants to actually *win*, they can't just say it's \"unsustainable\"—they need to tear apart the logic of the people proposing it. \n\nCan you go deeper on the \"dependency\" point? Frame it in a way that shows how UBI doesn't just \"risk\" making people dependent, but that it fundamentally undermines the social contract and the dignity of work. I want arguments that present the pro-UBI position as not just wrong, but as a dangerous fantasy that ignores how human society actually functions. Give me the most cutting, high-impact ways to frame that.",
